          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em homotopy coherent diagram
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commutativity
            is replaced by explicit
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            = succeed "ly" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent"} coherent
          %p
            It is a model for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          %p
            The idea perhaps intuitively makes sense but the management of the interactions between the various levels of homotopy requires care. The ideas were handled in various ways , but we will concentrate on approaches linked to the initial work of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"} Michael Boardman
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Rainer Vogt
            and then developed further by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"} Jean-Marc Cordier
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer"} Dwyer
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan"} Kan
          %p We will often use h.c. as an abbreviation for ‘’homotopy coherent’’.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_components In components
          %p
            The original definition of
            %a{:href => "#Vogt"} Vogt, 1973
            is essentially the following.
          %p
            Suppose now that we have the h.c. diagram
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : S(\mathbb{A}) \to \mathcal{B}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                to each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔸
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a)
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            %li
              %p
                for each string of composable
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔸
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma = (f_0, \ldots, f_n)
          %p
            starting at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and ending at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\sigma) : S(\mathbb{A})(0,n+1) \to \mathcal{B}(F(a), F(b)),
          %p that is, a higher homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\sigma) : \Delta[1]^n \to \mathcal{B}(F(a), F(b)),
          %p such that
          %p
            (i) if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0 = id
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mn 0
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi proj
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\sigma) = F(\partial_0\sigma)(proj \times \Delta[1]^{n-1})
          %p
            (ii) if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i = id
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\lt i \lt n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi i
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %mi m
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\sigma) = F(\partial_i\sigma(.(I^i \times m \times I^{n-i}),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m : I^2 \to I
            is the multiplicative structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \Delta[1]
            by the ‘max’ function on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
