                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mn 2
                              %mn 3
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{matrix}
                  X(1 3)X(0 1)&amp;\xrightarrow{X(1 2 3)X(0 1)}&amp;X(2 3)X(1 2)X(0 1)\\
                  \\mathllap{X(0 1 3)}\left\uparrow\space{30}{20}{0}\right.&amp; &amp;\left.\space{30}{20}{0}\right\uparrow\mathrlap{X(2 3) X(0 1 2)}\\
                  X(0 3)&amp;\xrightarrow[\qquad X(0 2 3)\qquad]{\quad}&amp;X(2 3)X(0 2)
                  \\end{matrix}
          %p and the diagram is made h.c. by specifying a second level homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0123
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(0123) : X(0)\times I^2\to X(3)
          %p filling this square, in the sense that restricting to each side of the square in the double homotopy gives the correspondingly labelled homotopy from the diagram.
          %p
            These can be continued for larger
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
          %h2#references_and_literature References and Literature
          %p
            For
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Vogt
          %ul
            %li#Vogt73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"}> Rainer Vogt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy limits and colimits
              %strong 134
              (1973) 11-52 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01219090"}> doi:10.1007/BF01219090
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/171965"} eudml:171965
          %p
            A generalisation of his theorem using simplicially enriched categories and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            of such a thing, is to be found in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.-M.+Cordier"} J.-M. Cordier
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T.+Porter"} T. Porter
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vogt’s Theorem on Categories of Homotopy Coherent Diagrams
          %p A neat application to changing objects in diagrams within a homotopy type can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              J.-M. Cordier and T. Porter,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Maps between homotopy coherent diagrams
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Kan"} Dan Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy commutative diagrams and their realizations
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(89)90023-6"} doi:10.1016/0022-4049(89)90023-6
          %p A summary of homotopy coherence can be found in Chapter 5 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Heiner+Kamps"}> Klaus Heiner Kamps
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract Homotopy and Simple Homotopy Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/2215"} doi:10.1142/2215
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.de/books?id=7JYKxInRMdAC&dq=Porter+Kamps&printsec=frontcover&source=bl&ots=uuyl_tIjs4&sig=Lt8I92xQBZ4DNKVXD0x76WkcxCE&hl=de&sa=X&oi=book_result&resnum=3&ct=result#PPP1,M1"} GoogleBooks
          %p and in chapter 10 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim Porter
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Crossed+Menagerie"} Crossed Menagerie
          %p The operad-theoretic description of homotopy-coherent diagrams is in
          %ul
            %li#BergerMoerdijkAlgebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Resolution of coloured operads and rectification of homotopy algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0512576"}> arXiv:math/0512576
              )
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on algebras over an operad
            for more on this.
